{"type":"message","id":"590943ac","parentId":"43a4c9a0","timestamp":"2026-04-10T14:32:04.150Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The system doesn't have python3-venv available. Let me try a different approach - I can use the MiniMax API directly with curl or wget to test the image generation capability, since I have the API key from TOOLS.md.\n\nFrom TOOLS.md:\n- 方舟 Ark: `c961bb1d-bae4-499f-a249-9d42c11a89d0`\n\nWait, that's for Ark (Anthropic/OpenAI compatible), not MiniMax.\n\nActually, looking at the MiniMax Skills documentation, it says:\n- 中国大陆：`https://api.minimaxi.com`\n- 全球：`https://api.minimax.io`\n\nAnd I need an API key. But I don't have a MiniMax API key in my TOOLS.md.\n\nActually, looking more carefully at the MiniMax Token Plan documentation - this is a subscription service where you get API calls included. The API key should be the same one used for MiniMax services.\n\nBut I don't have a MiniMax API key in my TOOLS.md. The only keys I have are:\n- 方舟 Ark: c961bb1d-bae4-499f-a249-9d42c11a89d0\n\nLet me check if I can use the MiniMax API directly without installing the skill. But first, I should check if there's a MiniMax API key available.\n\nActually, looking at the context - the user said \"立即添加吧\" - they want me to add/install the skill. But the skill is just the SKILL.md file that describes how to use MiniMax API. The actual API calls would need an API key.\n\nLet me take a different approach - I'll create the SKILL.md for MiniMax Multimodal Toolkit in my skills directory, which is what the skill actually is. The skill definition file itself is what \"installation\" means for OpenClaw skills."},{"type":"text","text":"环境有限制，让我换个方式——直接把skill文件复制到我的skills目录：\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_k8w3madwage4_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"mkdir -p /home/gem/workspace/agent/workspace/skills/minimax-multimodal-toolkit\ncp /tmp/minimax-skills/skills/minimax-multimodal-toolkit/SKILL.md /home/gem/workspace/agent/workspace/skills/minimax-multimodal-toolkit/\necho \"SKILL.md 已复制\"\ncat /home/gem/workspace/agent/workspace/skills/minimax-multimodal-toolkit/SKILL.md | head -50"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"minimax-token-plan","model":"MiniMax-M2.7-highspeed","usage":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":0,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1775831509441,"responseId":"06283cd5a7dc1317615331890cdafd78"}}
{"type":"message","id":"61112b3d","parentId":"590943ac","timestamp":"2026-04-10T14:32:04.253Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_function_k8w3madwage4_1","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"SKILL.md 已复制\n---\nname: mmx-cli\ndescription: Use mmx to generate text, images, video, speech, and music via the MiniMax AI platform. Use when the user wants to create media content, chat with MiniMax models, perform web search, or manage MiniMax API resources from the terminal.\n---\n\n# MiniMax CLI — Agent Skill Guide\n\nUse `mmx` to generate text, images, video, speech, music, and perform web search via the MiniMax AI platform.\n\n## Prerequisites\n\n```bash\n# Install\nnpm install -g mmx-cli\n\n# Auth (persisted to ~/.mmx/credentials.json)\nmmx auth login --api-key sk-xxxxx\n\n# Or pass per-call\nmmx text chat --api-key sk-xxxxx --message \"Hello\"\n```\n\nRegion is auto-detected. Override with `--region global` or `--region cn`.\n\n---\n\n## Agent Flags\n\nAlways use these flags in non-interactive (agent/CI) contexts:\n\n| Flag | Purpose |\n|---|---|\n| `--non-interactive` | Fail fast on missing args instead of prompting |\n| `--quiet` | Suppress spinners/progress; stdout is pure data |\n| `--output json` | Machine-readable JSON output |\n| `--async` | Return task ID immediately (video generation) |\n| `--dry-run` | Preview the API request without executing |\n| `--yes` | Skip confirmation prompts |\n\n---\n\n## Commands\n\n### text chat\n\nChat completion. Default model: `MiniMax-M2.7`.\n\n```bash\nmmx text chat --message <text> [flags]\n```"}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":23,"aggregated":"SKILL.md 已复制\n---\nname: mmx-cli\ndescription: Use mmx to generate text, images, video, speech, and music via the MiniMax AI platform. Use when the user wants to create media content, chat with MiniMax models, perform web search, or manage MiniMax API resources from the terminal.\n---\n\n# MiniMax CLI — Agent Skill Guide\n\nUse `mmx` to generate text, images, video, speech, music, and perform web search via the MiniMax AI platform.\n\n## Prerequisites\n\n```bash\n# Install\nnpm install -g mmx-cli\n\n# Auth (persisted to ~/.mmx/credentials.json)\nmmx auth login --api-key sk-xxxxx\n\n# Or pass per-call\nmmx text chat --api-key sk-xxxxx --message \"Hello\"\n```\n\nRegion is auto-detected. Override with `--region global` or `--region cn`.\n\n---\n\n## Agent Flags\n\nAlways use these flags in non-interactive (agent/CI) contexts:\n\n| Flag | Purpose |\n|---|---|\n| `--non-interactive` | Fail fast on missing args instead of prompting |\n| `--quiet` | Suppress spinners/progress; stdout is pure data |\n| `--output json` | Machine-readable JSON output |\n| `--async` | Return task ID immediately (video generation) |\n| `--dry-run` | Preview the API request without executing |\n| `--yes` | Skip confirmation prompts |\n\n---\n\n## Commands\n\n### text chat\n\nChat completion. Default model: `MiniMax-M2.7`.\n\n```bash\nmmx text chat --message <text> [flags]\n```","cwd":"/home/gem/workspace/agent/workspace"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1775831524213}}
